              "type": "_accordion-row-dynamic",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Are your shoes really wide-fit?",
                "content": "<p>Yes. We have been making wide-fit footwear in Singapore since 1974, and our shoes are designed with broader feet in mind. A roomy, broad-front last gives your toes space to spread naturally instead of being squeezed together.</p>",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              }
            },
            "row_2": {
              "type": "_accordion-row-dynamic",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Will your shoes suit bunions?",
                "content": "<p>Our broad-front last is bunion-friendly, giving the front of the foot extra room so there is less pressure on the joint. Every foot is different, so if you have a painful bunion or a medical condition, it is worth checking with your podiatrist or doctor too.</p>",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              }
            },
            "row_3": {
              "type": "_accordion-row-dynamic",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Can I wear my own orthotics or insoles?",
                "content": "<p>Our memory-foam insoles are removable, so you can take them out and use your own orthotic or insole if you prefer. If you are unsure whether a particular style will suit yours, email us at <a href=\"mailto:hello@foottree.com\">hello@foottree.com</a> before you order.</p>",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              }
            },
            "row_4": {
              "type": "_accordion-row-dynamic",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "What other comfort features do your shoes have?",
                "content": "<p>Along with the broad-front last, our shoes have removable memory-foam insoles for cushioning and slip-resistant outsoles for steadier footing. Some styles also have tie-free laces, which make them quick to slip on and off without bending down.</p>",
